6. Assembler

This section presents a basic assembler that translates assembly instructions into 16-bit machine code executable by the computer. It recognises A- and C-instructions, parses their components, and converts operation, destination, and jump mnemonics into binary fields. This version supports only numerical addresses; symbolic labels, variables, and symbol-table processing are not implemented. 

Java source code of and assembler is located in the Java_assembler file. 
Source code - Assembler.java 

Main method is reading command line arguments for the "intputFile" that contains mnemonics. 

How to start the program: 
java Assembler Program.asm


Small test file is in the same folder. 